UID:853bef6e71a75a7c@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T220717Z
SEQUENCE:2026091422
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Party Children ***\n
 Party Children — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-t
 one camisole leotard Male: Black Tights\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\, no 
 ribbons Male: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Ha
 lf Up-Half Down\, Curls (natural or curled) Male: Neat and out of the ey
 es\; Accessories (BA provides): Hair Bows Male: N/A\; Prop (BA provides)
 : Dolls/Hobby Horse\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder m
 atching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease with 
 an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No
  fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dance
 r doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red li
 pstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone balle
 t shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care 
 while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notif
 y Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discove
 ry\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories 
 on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain fro
 m sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, m
 end\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage
  make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smud
 ging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of 
 spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment no
 t assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage
  while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costu
 mes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove a
 ll bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n
 • Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with 
 any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not 
 pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or st
 ain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
