  Scene\, Battle Scene\, Snow Scene) (Mandatory – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 9:30 AM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 9:15 AM.\nOn stage: 10:30 AM–11:00 AM.\nACT 
 I Student Matinee Performance (to recorded sound)\; NO COFFEE\, BON BON\
 , ANGELS.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA:
  Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive
  15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\,
  Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehearsals and Perfor
 mances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANG
 E — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal ar
 e the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1x
 WFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKE
 UP — Party Children ***\nParty Children — Costume (you provide): Pin
 k Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard Male: Black Tights\; Sho
 es: Pink Ballet Shoes\, no ribbons Male: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Li
 ght Stage Makeup\; Hair: Half Up-Half Down\, Curls (natural or curled) M
 ale: Neat and out of the eyes\; Accessories (BA provides): Hair Bows Mal
 e: N/A\; Prop (BA provides): Dolls/Hobby Horse\nLight Stage Makeup Instr
 uction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow 
 applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eye
 liner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be su
 re to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage ligh
 ts)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone 
 tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handl
 e costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate 
 fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume dam
 age at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never thr
 ow costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elas
 tic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• 
 Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or acces
 sory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take grea
 t care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n
 • Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n
 • Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handl
 e or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of w
 ater\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or f
 rom the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces an
 d wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned 
 bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wa
 rdrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or an
 ything that may damage or stain costumes.
